  "summary": "Spring WebFlux Sockets expose request headers on exceptions",
  "details": "A Spring WebFlux application that supports WebSocket connections may expose indirectly sensitive user information by including request headers in an exception reason.\n\nSpring Framework 7.0.0 - 7.0.8\nSpring Framework 6.2.0 - 6.2.19\nSpring Framework 6.1.0 - 6.1.28\nSpring Framework 6.0.0 - 6.0.30\nSpring Framework 5.3.0 - 5.3.49\nSpring Framework 5.2.25.RELEASE and earlier",
